TI  - IO-AutoMapper: Leveraging LLMs to Bind I/O Signal List Entries to Control Function Blocks in Industrial Automation
PY  - 2025
T2  - IEEE International Conference on Emerging Technologies and Factory Automation, ETFA
DO  - 10.1109/ETFA65518.2025.11205551
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105021830541?origin=resultslist
AD  - Abb Corporate Research Center, Mannheim, Germany
AB  - Automation engineering in process industries involves mapping IO list specifications for sensor and actuator signals to control function blocks from vendor libraries. Due to the non-standardized format and content of IO lists, it is challenging to automate this mapping as it involves interpreting unstructured data (e.g., signal descriptions). Previous approaches proposed mapping of IO list contents to common data schemas, such as ontologies or UML models, but did not provide means to automate the initial data import from heterogeneous input formats. We propose IO-AutoMapper, an LLM-supported method to automatically process spreadsheet IO lists and map their entries to control library function blocks. Experiments with five IO lists with 300 signals each showed more than 98% correct mappings and low LLM processing costs. While LLM hallucinations could not yet be fully eliminated, the method has the potential to reduce human labor for mapping IO list entries by more than 90%. © 2025 IEEE.
