AB  - The proceedings contain 40 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Model-Based Software and Systems Engineering. The topics include: Model-Based Assessment of Conformance to Acknowledged Security-Related Software Architecture Good Practices; the Lifecycle of Data Clumps: A Longitudinal Case Study in Open-Source Projects; Comparative Evaluation of NLP Approaches for Requirements Formalisation; torque not Work, Representing Kinds of Quantities; System Architects Are not Alone Anymore: Automatic System Modeling with AI; fault Tree Reliability Analysis via Squarefree Polynomials; MDE-Based Graphical Tool for Modeling Data Provenance According to the W3C PROV Standard; Coding by Design: GPT-4 Empowers Agile Model Driven Development; an Analysis and Simulation Framework for Systems with Classification Components; virtual61850: A Model-Driven Tool to Support the Design and Validation of Virtualized Controllers in Power Industry; Defining KPIs for Executable DSLs: A Manufacturing System Case Study; multi-Dimensional Process Analysis of Software Development Projects; cycle-Accurate Virtual Prototyping with Multiplicity; kant: A Domain-Specific Language for Modeling Security Protocols; large Language Models in Enterprise Modeling: Case Study and Experiences; Jabuti CE: A Tool for Specifying Smart Contracts in the Domain of Enterprise Application Integration; qualitative Reasoning and Design Space Exploration; constructive Assertions with Abstract Models; Single-Sourcing for Desktop and Web Applications with EMF Parsley; AI-Based Recognition of Sketched Class Diagrams; On Augmenting Scenario-Based Modeling with Generative AI; model-Driven Methodology for Developing Chatbots Based on Microservice Architecture; using Personalised Authentication Flows to Address Issues with Traditional Authentication Methods; a Tool for Modeling and Tailoring Hybrid Software Processes; towards a Domain Model for Learning and Teaching.
