AU  - Karmakar, R.
AU  - Maurya, S.K.
TI  - AI-based navigation browser extension for AWS
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of 2026 1st International Conference on Intelligent Computing and Automation for Sustainable Solutions, ICASS 2026
DO  - 10.1109/ICASS69550.2026.11547549
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105042936651?origin=resultslist
AD  - Chandigarh University, Dept. Of Computer Science Engineering With Specialzation With Aiml, Punjab, India
AD  - Chandigarh University, Ait Cse, Punjab, India
AB  - The proposed system dives into the creation and deployment of an AI enhanced extension to the Navigation Assistant which aims to simplify user communications with Amazon AWS Management console using a web browser. By using carefully tuned large language models (LLMs) on AWS Bedrock, the system offers AWS domain context-aware, step-by-step guidance for hackers to cloud complexities, flattens the learning curve for new users and boosts productivity among pros. Fundamentally, the paper dissects the use of Fine-tuning contrast to Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) in study implying that fine-tuning domesticates domain knowledge on faster, more accurate answers while RAG replenishes the ephemeral or always changing information. We have a multi-tiered pipeline for data preprocessing which builds the training datasets from its roots, AWS documentation, support forums and synthetic data. The implementation involved two architectural solutions: AWS Bedrock fine-tuned production-grade model in the other, and Llama.cpp local rapid prototyping setup to compare performance, scalability and security. Modern engineering practices (UML modelling, CI/ CD pipelines, automated test tools) enabled thorough model accuracy and response latency testing and verification in conjunction with comprehensive testing/validation methodologies to enforce deployment robustness. The results show substantial better navigation (an average of 38.7% better than the base model) and user pleasure (4.6/5), but also reveal challenges for immediate UI element interaction, model drift prevention and aggressive fine-tuning-RAG optimization in hybrid. This research is the first scalable technical navigation framework with a solution for LLM tuning, cloud automation and secure AI deployment in enterprise environments.  © 2026 IEEE.
