AD  - Faculty of Computer Science and Engineering, Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology (HCMUT), 268 Ly Thuong Kiet Street, Dien Hong Ward, Ho Chi Minh City, Viet Nam
AD  - Vietnam National University Ho Chi Minh City (VNU-HCM), Linh Xuan Ward, Ho Chi Minh City, Viet Nam
AB  - Transforming natural language requirements into structured use case diagrams and scenarios remains labor-intensive despite recent advances in Large Language Models. Existing pipelines often lack transparency, struggle with complex relationships, and provide limited support for human correction. To address these issues, we propose a Human-in-the-Loop multi-agent framework that combines automated reasoning with targeted human oversight. The framework employs a Requirement Parsing Agent to extract actors and use cases, and a Scenario Generation Agent to produce and evaluate scenarios using a multi-judge mechanism assessing completeness, correctness, and relevance. Human validation is integrated at key stages to ensure structural and semantic alignment. Evaluation across multiple software systems shows improved element coverage and relationship identification compared to commercial tools, demonstrating the effectiveness of combining agent-based automation with human expertise. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2027.
