AB  - This paper outlines the design of an Online Research Ethics Management Information System (REMIS) specifically tailored for Open and Distance Learning (ODL) Institutions, using Botswana Open University as a case study. The system is designed to streamline the ethical review and approval process for research proposals, thereby ensuring compliance with ethical standards and regulations. The proposed design model encompasses features such as online submission and tracking of research proposals, automated notifications, integration with generative artificial intelligence for user queries, and advanced reporting capabilities. The system was developed using a variety of technologies with an emphasis on systems design and performance. The paper further covers theoretical background, brief related work, the methodology employed for the system's development and shares study insights. © 2025 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
