AB  - The proceedings contain 12 papers. The topics discussed include: analyzing toxicity in open-source software communications using psycholinguistics and moral foundations theory; SkillScope: a tool to predict fine-grained skills needed to solve issues on GitHub; synthesizing access control policies using large language models; semantic API alignment: linking high-level user goals to APIs; evaluating the performance and efficiency of sentence-BERT for code comment classification; automating benchmark generation for LLMs in software engineering: challenges and opportunities; code comment classification with data augmentation and transformer-based models; GRAPHiC: utilizing graph structures and class weights in code comment classification with pretrained BERT models; evaluating large language models in exercises of UML use case diagrams modeling; and optimizing deep learning models to address class imbalance in code comment classification.
